Let $P=\sum_{i=0}^{D_1}a_ix^i$, $Q=\sum_{j=0}^{D_2}b_jx^j$ with $a_{D_1}
ot\equiv0$, $b_{D_2}
ot\equiv0\pmod p$. Then $PQ=a_{D_1}b_{D_2}x^{D_1+D_2}+(	ext{terms of lower degree})$. Since $p$ is prime and $p
mid a_{D_1}$, $p
mid b_{D_2}$, we have $p
mid a_{D_1}b_{D_2}$. So the coefficient of $x^{D_1+D_2}$ is nonzero mod $p$ and $\deg PQ=D_1+D_2$. $ lacksquare$
